AI coding agent

Usage: opi [OPTIONS] [PROMPT]... [COMMAND]

Commands:
  package  Manage extension packages
  doctor   Summarize local health across config, provider, package, session, tui, rpc
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [PROMPT]...
          Initial prompt (positional)

Options:
  -m, --model <MODEL>
          Model spec, e.g. anthropic:claude-sonnet-4

  -c, --config <CONFIG>
          Config file path

  -s, --system <SYSTEM>
          System prompt file

      --non-interactive
          Single prompt mode (non-interactive)

      --allow-mutating
          Allow mutating tools (write, edit, bash) in non-interactive mode

      --trust
          Trust this project and load its project resources (`.opi/config.toml`, project skills/fragments/themes/extensions, project packages, and project `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`). Mutually exclusive with `--no-trust`. Overrides `[defaults] default_project_trust` and the trust store

      --no-trust
          Do not trust this project; skip its project resources (user-global resources and explicit `--config`/`--system-prompt` still apply, tools are unchanged). Mutually exclusive with `--trust`

      --execution-backend <BACKEND>
          Execution backend override for `command.execute`: `local` (built-in) or an installed adapter id. Selects the `fixed` strategy. This is a routing override only — it cannot grant trust or permission. Overrides `[execution] backend` from layered TOML

      --execution-strategy <STRATEGY>
          Execution routing strategy override: `fixed`, `rules`, or `model`. This is a routing override only — it cannot grant trust or permission. Overrides `[execution] strategy` from layered TOML
          
          [possible values: fixed, rules, model]

      --json
          Output NDJSON events to stdout (non-interactive mode)

      --json-compact
          Compact `--json` output: streamed `text_delta` updates omit the redundant cumulative snapshot, making long streamed turns ~linear in bytes. Default `--json` output is unchanged

      --rpc
          RPC JSONL mode: bidirectional command/event protocol over stdin/stdout

      --list-sessions
          List all sessions

      --resume <RESUME>
          Resume a session by ID

      --fork <FORK>
          Fork a session by ID into a new session

      --delete-session <DELETE_SESSION>
          Delete a session by ID

      --export-session <ID_OR_PATH>
          Export a session to a local markdown or json file and exit. The argument is a session id resolved against the sessions directory, or a path to a session JSONL file (Phase 13.5)

      --output <PATH>
          Output file path for `--export-session`. Required when exporting

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format for `--export-session`. Default: markdown
          
          [default: markdown]
          [possible values: markdown, json]

      --full-tree
          Export the full branch tree instead of just the active branch

      --exclude-tool-output
          Omit tool result output from the export

      --exclude-thinking
          Omit assistant thinking content from the export

      --redact <MODE>
          Redaction mode for `--export-session`: summary, verbose, or none. Default: summary

          Possible values:
          - summary: Phase 7 `Summary`: scrub secrets, content-sensitive fields, and absolute paths. Safe-by-default
          - verbose: Phase 7 `Verbose`: scrub secrets and content-sensitive fields, keep absolute paths
          - none:    Skip redaction entirely. Only for trusted-local contexts where the export never leaves the host
          
          [default: summary]

      --generate-completion <SHELL>
          Generate shell completions to stdout
          
          [possible values: bash, zsh, fish, powershell, elvish]

  -v, --verbose
          Enable debug tracing

      --trace <PATH>
          Write each run's evidence.jsonl + manifest.json under PATH (interactive, non-interactive, JSON, and RPC; 0.x unstable, opt-in)

      --tools <TOOLS>
          Tool allowlist (comma-separated, e.g. "read,glob")

      --no-tools
          Disable all tools

      --no-builtin-tools
          Disable built-in tools (reserved for Phase 4 extension tools)

      --image <IMAGE>
          Attach image file(s) to the prompt

      --list-models
          List available models and exit

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Tool policy:
  Interactive mode enables read, write, edit, and bash.
  Non-interactive/RPC mode defaults to read, grep, find, ls, and glob.
  write, edit, and bash require --allow-mutating or defaults.allow_mutating_tools = true outside interactive mode.
  --no-tools disables all tools; --tools is an allowlist; --no-builtin-tools removes built-ins.

Bash policy:
  bash runs one foreground command from the workspace root.
  Windows uses cmd /C; Unix uses sh -c.
  The default timeout is 30 seconds; timeout_secs overrides it per call.
  Combined stdout/stderr are capped at 64 KiB. Larger output sets truncated and may write the complete output path in details.full_output.
  This is a tool-selection check, not a permission popup or sandbox subsystem.

Execution policy:
  --execution-backend local|<adapter-id> selects the fixed command.execute backend.
  --execution-strategy fixed|rules|model selects the routing strategy.
  Both are routing overrides only: they cannot grant package trust or adapter permission.
  Capability permission ([execution.permissions]) is read from the USER config only; project permission sections are rejected.
  --allow-mutating gates bash tool availability independently from adapter permission.

Interactive authentication:
  /login <provider> starts login for Anthropic, GitHub Copilot, or OpenAI Codex.
  /logout <provider> deletes that provider's stored credential.
  Non-interactive, JSON, and RPC modes never start login; CredentialNeeded reports the provider and /login remediation.
